{
  "task": {
    "id": "Prob113_2012_q1g",
    "spec": "\r\nI would like you to implement a module named TopModule with the following\r\ninterface. All input and output ports are one bit unless otherwise\r\nspecified.\r\n\r\n - input  x (4 bits)\r\n - output f\r\n\r\nThe module should implement the function f shown in the Karnaugh map\r\nbelow.\r\n\r\n             x[0]x[1]\r\nx[2]x[3]  00  01  11  10\r\n  00     | 1 | 0 | 0 | 1 |\r\n  01     | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\r\n  11     | 1 | 1 | 1 | 0 |\r\n  10     | 1 | 1 | 0 | 1 |\r\n\r\n",
    "interface": {
      "top": "TopModule",
      "ports": [
        {
          "name": "x",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 4,
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "f",
          "direction": "output",
          "width": 1,
          "signed": false
        }
      ]
    },
    "constraints": "SystemVerilog, exactly one self-contained TopModule DUT. Inline all helper logic inside TopModule; do not define auxiliary modules. xczu3eg-sbva484-1-e; 5 ns synthesis clock; simulator seed 1. No reference dependencies, hierarchy outside the DUT, file access, includes or DPI."
  },
  "sample_id": "f9e8f9e6-8d4e-46f3-9ae5-27a215caf88c",
  "variant_id": "C",
  "current": {
    "revision_id": "90d4858c-2b40-4eaa-b56c-d4beda7ff452",
    "source_sha256": "06c63785b0c037e69daee5f7c8204707e270c5d76cc4c71b4bda099d45540655",
    "source": "module TopModule (\n    input  [3:0] x,\n    output       f\n);\n    assign f = (~x[3] & ~x[1])\n             | (~x[3] &  x[2] & ~x[0])\n             | ( x[3] &  x[2] & ~x[0])\n             | ( x[3] &  x[2] &  x[1]);\nendmodule\n"
  },
